Subject: [PATCH 38/39] ZoneRebalance: landing edits (status text, the
 published ZoneContents.ext', the sketches)

The module's status paragraph, its Main results entry and the TuringMachine facade no longer call
the two rows sorried. The private zr_contents_ext is removed: its four uses cite the published
Turing.ZoneContents.ext' (the same statement). The two rows' construction sketches describe the
proofs taken: the column moves cut the scratch copy instead of re-packing it, and the extension
row's ruler is copied from the last field.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
